[
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# Edge to Cloud Broker Bridge — solution\n\nDeploy the clean UNS, edge alert, local demo bridge, and cloud access Rules. Simulation lives in a separate notebook so production users never need to delete demo code.\n\n**Operators:** README **Production readiness** (Rules first on the cloud broker; omit the simulator; use the TLS production notebook for WAN).  \n**Maintainers:** see `AUTHORING.md` for design decisions and how to extend this template.\n\n## Included execution targets\n\n| Section | Run against |\n|---|---|\n| Models and Actions | **Edge** broker (`localhost:1883` with Compose) |\n| Demo Route | **Edge** broker, after creating the cloud bridge user and setting the edge secret/env |\n| Rules | **Cloud** broker (`localhost:1884` with Compose) |\n\n## Demo sequence (hardware-free)\n\n1. Run Models and Actions on the edge.\n2. Run `edge-cloud-bridge-simulator.lotnb` on the edge.\n3. Set edge secret/env, then enable the demo Route.\n4. Apply Rules on the cloud broker.\n\n## Production sequence\n\nDo not run the simulator. Apply cloud Rules first, deploy edge Models and Actions, then use `edge-cloud-bridge-production.lotnb` instead of the local demo Route. Full checklist: README Production readiness.\n\n## Architecture\n\n```\nraw/factory/... → Models → factory/... (clean UNS) → alert Action\n                                      ↓\n                         MQTT_BRIDGE (DIRECTION out)\n                                      ↓\n                    sites/site-plant/factory/... (cloud)\n```"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Models\n\nMap raw hall-A machine signals into clean UNS JSON under `factory/hall-a/<machine>/reading`. The bridge later prefixes this subtree to `sites/site-plant/...`.\n\n**Reads:** `raw/factory/hall-a/machine1/{temperature,state,id}`  \n**Writes:** `factory/hall-a/machine1/reading`"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE MODEL HallAMachine1Reading WITH TOPIC \"factory/hall-a/machine1/reading\"\n    ADD STRING \"site_id\" WITH \"site-plant\"\n    ADD STRING \"area\" WITH \"hall-a\"\n    ADD STRING \"machine_id\" WITH TOPIC \"raw/factory/hall-a/machine1/id\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature\" WITH TOPIC \"raw/factory/hall-a/machine1/temperature\" AS TRIGGER\n    ADD STRING \"state\" WITH TOPIC \"raw/factory/hall-a/machine1/state\"\n    ADD STRING \"unit\" WITH \"celsius\"\n    ADD STRING \"timestamp\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"UTC\""
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "Same raw→clean mapping for machine 2 so the bridge and cloud Rules see more than one device.\n\n**Reads:** `raw/factory/hall-a/machine2/{temperature,state,id}`  \n**Writes:** `factory/hall-a/machine2/reading`"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE MODEL HallAMachine2Reading WITH TOPIC \"factory/hall-a/machine2/reading\"\n    ADD STRING \"site_id\" WITH \"site-plant\"\n    ADD STRING \"area\" WITH \"hall-a\"\n    ADD STRING \"machine_id\" WITH TOPIC \"raw/factory/hall-a/machine2/id\"\n    ADD DOUBLE \"temperature\" WITH TOPIC \"raw/factory/hall-a/machine2/temperature\" AS TRIGGER\n    ADD STRING \"state\" WITH TOPIC \"raw/factory/hall-a/machine2/state\"\n    ADD STRING \"unit\" WITH \"celsius\"\n    ADD STRING \"timestamp\" WITH TIMESTAMP \"UTC\""
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Actions\n\nEdge-side high-temperature alert so a 5-minute demo has something observable before you look at the cloud topics. Threshold: **85 °C**.\n\n**Reads:** `factory/hall-a/+/reading`  \n**Writes:** `factory/hall-a/<machine>/alert/high_temp` (non-retained event)"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ACTION HallAHighTempAlert\nON TOPIC \"factory/hall-a/+/reading\" DO\n    SET \"machine_id\" WITH TOPIC POSITION 3\n    SET \"temperature\" WITH (GET JSON \"temperature\" IN PAYLOAD AS DOUBLE)\n    IF {temperature} > 85 THEN\n        PUBLISH TOPIC \"factory/hall-a/\" + {machine_id} + \"/alert/high_temp\" WITH (\"High temperature on \" + {machine_id} + \": \" + {temperature} + \" C\")"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Routes\n\n> **Requires a reachable cloud broker.** Safe to skip while you only validate the Simulator + Models on the edge. With Compose, the cloud service hostname is `coreflux-cloud` on port `1883` inside the Docker network (host port `1884`).\n\nCreates the edge→cloud MQTT Bridge: forwards clean UNS `factory/#` to `sites/site-plant/factory/#` with `DIRECTION \"out\"`. Password comes from the edge secret store; host from an env var (never put a URL scheme in a secret).\n\n**Before running this cell on the edge broker**, publish to `$SYS/Coreflux/Command`:\n- `-setEnv CLOUD_BROKER_HOST=coreflux-cloud`\n- `-setSecret BRIDGE_SITE_PLANT_PASSWORD=<same password as the cloud bridge user>`\n"
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE ROUTE EdgeToCloudBridge WITH TYPE MQTT_BRIDGE\n    ADD SOURCE_CONFIG\n        WITH BROKER SELF\n    ADD DESTINATION_CONFIG\n        WITH BROKER_ADDRESS GET ENV \"CLOUD_BROKER_HOST\"\n        WITH BROKER_PORT '1883'\n        WITH CLIENT_ID \"edge-site-plant-bridge\"\n        WITH USERNAME \"bridge_site_plant\"\n        WITH PASSWORD GET SECRET \"BRIDGE_SITE_PLANT_PASSWORD\"\n        WITH USE_TLS \"false\"\n        WITH RECONNECTION_RETRIES '20'\n    ADD MAPPING siteFactoryOut\n        WITH SOURCE_TOPIC \"factory/#\"\n        WITH DESTINATION_TOPIC \"sites/site-plant/factory/#\"\n        WITH DIRECTION \"out\""
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "## Rules\n\n**Run these cells on the cloud broker only.**\n\nNotebook order puts Rules last on purpose: a deny-by-default set applied mid-notebook on the edge could lock the deploying identity out of remaining cells. In production, deploy cloud Rules **before** enabling the edge bridge (see README Production readiness).\n\nMid-session effect of new Rules on already-connected clients is not fully documented; treat as applying to subsequent publish/subscribe operations and re-test after deploy.\n\n### User story: site bridge publisher\n\n`bridge_site_plant` may publish under `sites/site-plant/#` and is denied under the broader `sites/#` tree (so it cannot write another site's namespace). Create the user on the cloud broker first: publish `-addUser bridge_site_plant <password>` to `$SYS/Coreflux/Command`."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE RULE AllowSitePlantBridgePublish WITH PRIORITY 20 FOR Publish TO TOPIC \"sites/site-plant/#\"\n    IF USER IS \"bridge_site_plant\" OR USER IS \"root\" THEN\n        ALLOW\n    ELSE\n        DENY"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "Deny the site-plant bridge user from publishing anywhere else under `sites/#`. Priority **30** (lower precedence than the allow above) so `sites/site-plant/...` still matches the allow rule first."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE RULE DenySitePlantBridgeOutsideSite WITH PRIORITY 30 FOR Publish TO TOPIC \"sites/#\"\n    IF USER IS \"bridge_site_plant\" THEN\n        DENY\n    ELSE\n        ALLOW"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "### User story: read-only site dashboard\n\n`dashboard_site` may subscribe to the site subtree but must not publish into it. Create the user with `-addUser dashboard_site <password>` on the cloud broker.\n\nSubscribe allow (priority 20), then an explicit publish deny at priority **15** (evaluated before the bridge publish allow) with no ELSE so non-dashboard users fall through to the site publish rules above."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE RULE AllowSiteDashboardSubscribe WITH PRIORITY 20 FOR Subscribe TO TOPIC \"sites/site-plant/#\"\n    IF USER IS \"dashboard_site\" OR USER IS \"root\" OR USER IS \"bridge_site_plant\" THEN\n        ALLOW\n    ELSE\n        DENY"
  },
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "Deny publishes from the dashboard user into the site tree (priority 15, deny-only when the user matches)."
  },
  {
    "kind": 2,
    "language": "lot",
    "value": "DEFINE RULE DenySiteDashboardPublish WITH PRIORITY 15 FOR Publish TO TOPIC \"sites/site-plant/#\"\n    IF USER IS \"dashboard_site\" THEN\n        DENY"
  }
]